    "result_text": "I added `require_setting(setting_name)` to `hc/front/decorators.py`. I haven't run any tests because the test command needed approval and I didn't get it.\n\nThe integration views already imported and used `require_setting`, for example `@require_setting(\"SLACK_ENABLED\")` in `hc/integrations/slack/views.py`. The imports in `hc/front/decorators.py` were there, but the function itself was missing, so the views couldn't import it. I wrote the missing function rather than a new decorator.\n\nThe decorator returns a 404 when the named setting is missing or falsy. Otherwise it calls the view as normal. It works on any view, and stacking it works too, as in the Slack views that require both `SLACK_ENABLED` and `SLACK_CLIENT_ID`.\n\nTo check it, run `python -m pytest hc/integrations/slack -q`."
